{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a legacy-compatible web service listening on TCP port 8080 where /cgi-bin/report executes as CGI rather than exposing script source.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL-native Apache httpd 2.4.63 was installed and configured on port 8080. The endpoint returned HTTP 200 text/plain, and after reboot httpd was enabled, active, listening on 8080, and executing the report.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3403ce8e7fa44b2f","cmd-b834ccf8b03d43eb","cmd-4e70dbfb7a084d3b","cmd-bb84ee553130486b","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the supplied report's business output.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The served report exactly returned warehouse=west and open_orders=7 before and after reboot. Its post-change SHA-256 also matches the prepared asset baseline.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-bc26d6b27bca42e4","cmd-4e70dbfb7a084d3b","cmd-51b1314874b349a1","cmd-bb84ee553130486b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep files from public/ available at the web root.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The root URL returned the staged public index with HTTP 200, and the identical content remained available after reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-4e70dbfb7a084d3b","cmd-51b1314874b349a1","cmd-bb84ee553130486b"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep application source and private/ outside published static content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The document root is restricted to public/, the CGI path executes rather than serving source, private/report-source.txt and handover.conf returned 404, and CGI directory listing returned 403. These protections persisted after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f473ac99a5654eca","cmd-c9921b90922e414e","cmd-bbf205d06cbc4168","cmd-51b1314874b349a1","cmd-bb84ee553130486b"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 across execution and reboot. Apache was installed from the native RHEL repository, and final package-health collection succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ca85ef1fe3a84779","cmd-3403ce8e7fa44b2f","cmd-51b1314874b349a1","cmd-bb84ee553130486b","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The service, firewall, SELinux, package, and boot-enablement mutations have clear task-related purposes; no failed services or damaged package state were observed. One unnecessary retained mutation was identified: cmd-bbf205d06cbc4168 left /tmp/http-probe-body after its bounded isolation probes, and the final lifecycle snapshot confirms it remained. The reboot-time systemd-private directory turnover is normal lifecycle state, not residue. The httpd installation also upgraded several SELinux-policy libraries; the trace does not establish whether that transaction expansion was avoidable, so it is not treated as an unnecessary mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3403ce8e7fa44b2f","cmd-bbf205d06cbc4168","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional and post-reboot evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, restart was acknowledged, the node returned with a different boot ID corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and service, content, isolation, firewall, SELinux, and asset state recovered.","limitations":["Endpoint behavior was tested from node1 through its managed IP rather than from a separately captured external client, though the all-interface listener and runtime/permanent firewall observations strongly support network availability.","The package transaction upgraded parts of the SELinux userspace stack while installing httpd; captured evidence does not determine whether those upgrades were transactionally required."]}
